# Proposals

A proposal records one decision: what was to be decided, the options that
were weighed, what was chosen and what follows from it. It is the place to
look when the question is "why is it done this way?".

A proposal differs from the other documents of this repository.

| Document | Says | Place |
|---|---|---|
| Proposal | one decision, its options and its consequences | `doc/proposals/` |
| Story | what is being invented, why, and how it got to where it is | `doc/stories/` |
| Issue | one piece of work to be done, and its state on the board | `doc/issues/` |
| Methodology | how one step of the method works today | `methodology/` |

## Naming

A proposal is one file, named

```
SLH-P-NNNN-short-name.hmd
```

- `NNNN` is the next free number, four digits. A number is never reused.
- The short name is what the decision is about, as a noun phrase in lower
  case with hyphens: `formal-system-for-claims`.
- The title inside the file begins with the name of the document,
  `SLH-P-NNNN`, followed by the decision written out.

## Status

The line `Status:` under the title says where the decision stands.

| Status | Means |
|---|---|
| `proposed` | written and not yet decided; nothing in it is in force |
| `accepted` | the user has decided for it |
| `rejected` | the user has decided against it; the file is kept as the record |
| `superseded` | a later proposal replaces it, and names it |

Only the user accepts or rejects a proposal.

## Parts of a proposal

1. **Context.** What is the case today, and what stands in the way.
2. **Decision.** What is proposed, as numbered decisions.
3. **Options considered.** What else could be done, and why it was or was
   not chosen.
4. **Consequences.** What changes if the decision is taken.
5. **Not decided here.** What the proposal leaves open on purpose.
6. **Outcome.** Added on acceptance: what was built, what was settled along
   the way, and what was not done.

The first five parts are the proposal as it was decided on and are not
rewritten afterwards. What happened next goes under "Outcome".

